      "vision_by": "pick:cloud-claude-sonnet-5",
      "vision_reason": "A wooden fish club with a carved human face head in Northwest Coast style, an object type used by Kwakwaka'wakw and neighboring peoples for dispatching fish; the record only describes it as \"southern Northwest Coast style\" without independent attribution evidence, but this is a widely-shared regional tool form consistent with the claimed group.",
